WEBVTT

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.130
Justice is but the aggregate interests of the common good.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.740
History is nothing more than a record book written for the convenience of its author.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.280
Blessed are those who cherish each other, or so we thought.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.760
So much interference working against us.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.450
Taking with us the goodwill that they would cast out,

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.300
we left the ship behind.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.680
Nergal - Hiratsuka Dock

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:55.220
A Place We Call "Home"

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.630
Three more days to finish the check on the engine block and the phase transition cannon.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.450
Training the replacement crew will require another ten days.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.370
So it will be another two weeks.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.060
Skip the training.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.630
Launch the ship as soon as we finish all the check procedures.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:07.750
That won't be possible.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.520
Half the crew may have stayed with us, but with them like that...

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.940
That's why we have the replacement crew.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.940
This issue has been dealt with, right?

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.960
Yes, Sir. Their personalities do not present a problem.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:20.510
But in exchange, they lack many of the required abilities.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:23.200
Well, at least we won't have a mutiny on our hands.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.120
The third ship is ready as well.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.970
With the Earth mostly rid of the Jovian Lizard threat,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.050
the UEAF appear to be in high spirits

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.220
as they prepare their major counterattack.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.410
With us is the commanding officer of the UESF 3rd Fleet,

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.800
Misumaru Kouichirou-san...

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.690
Are you going to spend all your time in front of the TV?

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.160
We're going to open the shop soon.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.650
But my father was on.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:47.520
Are you going to skip work?

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.940
Yes, I'm coming.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.350
Sweet and sour pork combo!

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.140
Miso ramen!

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:52.640
Salt ramen!

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.560
Fried rice and fried dumplings!

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.580
Quing jiaxo rou shin!

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:54.930
Hui guo rou!

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:55.720
I'll have the miso ramen!

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.320
Me too!

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.730
Tang mein, and make it extra large.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.280
I'll repeat the order.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.930
Starting from you, Sir... Sweet and sour pork combo, miso ramen.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.700
Salt, soy sauce, and fried rice with fried dumplings.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.230
Qing jiaxo rou shin and hui guo rou. You'll have the lunch set?

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.130
Miso, miso, tang mein, and you'll have it extra large.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.310
Will that be all?

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:14.560
Hey, she's pretty good.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.340
Isn't she?

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.130
She did graduate from the UEAF University Strategic Sim Program at the top of her class.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.540
That's the first time I've seen her actually being helpful.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.660
What are you saying?!

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.080
Yurika went about being the captain of the Nadesico honorably.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.350
And honorably we ended up like this.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.120
Well, there was stupidity on our part as well.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.730
You try to be a superhero, only to find out Earth doesn't want one.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.870
Hey! What's the point of spacing out while looking at the soup!?

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.440
Start getting the ramen ready!

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.880
And you, stop wandering around while you wash dishes!

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:43.800
And wash this!

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:44.080
Yes, Sir.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.380
I can't believe what I touched with it.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:45.870
Sweet and sour pork's ready!

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:46.790
Be right there!

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.450
Come on! We've got a lot of dishes to pump out!

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.080
Yes, Sir.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.630
Oh, such a beautiful laundry day!

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:54.800
Laundry day?

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.710
It means the weather is perfect to dry your laundry outside.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:00.860
On the Nadesico, we could only use the dryer,

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.640
but it's much better when you can sun dry it.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.060
When you dry it with the sun and natural wind...

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.640
See! All soft!

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.340
I just love sunny days.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:15.750
Right?

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.150
I guess I could live with you.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:24.440
Peek...

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:25.660
I was just...

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.330
Well, I'm still not happy about it, but...

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.420
Some Earthlings are all right.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.300
There are a lot of bad ones too.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.510
If we could only find someway of getting a hold of everyone.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.280
Why file a report after all that's happened?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.020
I'm not anxious to go through this.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.610
Investigations take time.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.610
And the UEAF has been nagging us for a full report.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:03.090
So, before we release an official Nergal statement,

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:05.330
I thought it'd be best to have the chairman go through it.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.600
Goat Hory...

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.310
We'll have to figure out how you should be treated as well.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.500
Well, I'll figure it out soon.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.940
So how is our gang doing?

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.960
I wouldn't think they could do much anymore.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.400
One hundred fifteen people left the Nadesico in the confusion.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.630
Four remain unaccounted for.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.080
In the four weeks since the incident, twenty have returned to their former occupations.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.670
Thirteen have requested to be reinstated on the Nadesico.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:33.310
The rest are hiding out. We do have them under supervision.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.230
I'll leave you to monitor their movements.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:38.990
It certainly is nice that the most dangerous characters are all bunched up together.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.570
It's hard to imagine that they fought the Jovians for so long.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:44.490
But if push comes to shove, don't hesitate to have them neutralized.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:48.760
It seems that they're amiable to not being amiable at all.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.270
Pros-san, where does this book go?

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:54.750
Pros-san, I can't find the shelf for the 1990s!

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:58.430
Pros-san, why does the Nergal bulletin have comics inside it?

00:05:59.070 --> 00:05:59.740
These girls are too young for this kind of demotion.

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:01.340
Elise, please be quiet.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.250
Right, leave this to me.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.430
Lychee Lycheru Lycheolla Lychee!

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.560
Thank you for coming!

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.000
Natural Lychee! Remember these words well.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:10.720
This voice..

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.680
Is it Megu-chan's?

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.390
Evil never perishes. Justice is always fickle.

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.500
I won't forgive you, Rambutan!

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:16.640
I will not let you...

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.350
Earth shall become the domain of the Jovan!

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:24.590
Okay.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.160
Thank you for your direction!

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:27.450
Good work.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:28.570
Megumi-chan!

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:29.760
Producer!

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.550
I'm so glad you came back!

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:31.870
Thank you.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.690
Megumi-chan's Rambutan is wonderful. The director is happy too.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:36.660
It's really good.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.840
Thank you very much.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.190
Thanks for all the work.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.140
Ah, Mari-chan, thank you.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:42.490
Mari-san...

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.050
You want to be taken off Natural Lychee?

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.530
I can't thank the producer and the director enough

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.490
for allowing me to play such a significant role,

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.980
even through I came out of nowhere all of a sudden, but...

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.560
Natural Lychee these days...

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.900
It just isn't the same anymore. They're fighting all the time.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.130
That's because...

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:01.570
Because it's wartime?

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.480
Why did we have to use a name like Jovan for the bad guys?

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.530
It's so obvious.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:10.130
We need anime that's more free-spirited and fun, instead.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.490
Why did it have to become a fighting anime?

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:17.000
But thanks to that, we have the character Rambutan.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.430
I think she's very interesting, thanks to you.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:24.420
You should just give your best in acting, like you are doing now.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:25.590
But...

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.310
That's for your benefit as well.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.010
I think Erina would say the same thing too.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.910
It's been a while, Megu-chan.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:34.780
Thanks for the message.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:35.820
You can't imagine how surprised I was.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:38.110
I never realized that you and Megumi-chan were acquaintances.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:40.190
Do you know each other?

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.740
We'll use all the resources of Nergal to back up your career.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.660
You don't have to worry about anything except acting. Understood?

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:54.030
You are not to mention anything about Mars and Jupiter.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.820
Just give everything you have to playing the part of Rambutan.

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.060
The ratings for the Jovan season have been wonderful.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.890
We're proud to be the sponsor for this show.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.920
You won't get far running away from us!

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.250
Normally, all the former crew of the Nadesico

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.980
would be considered criminals!

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.600
I...

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:28.280
Megumi-chan!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.130
Hey, will you come along with me?

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:36.120
I think we have too much static around here.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.050
I just want to talk to Megu-chan!

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:42.710
Megumi-chan, over here!

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:43.620
Over here!

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:50.920
So, I've been under surveillance all this time?

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:51.760
That's right.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.120
Not just you.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:57.550
But the entire crew of the Nadesico is under Nergal surveillance, as best as they can.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:58.350
As best as they can?

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:02.090
I hear that there are quite a few still on the run.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:05.830
In those cases, it's more like searching and investigating, instead of surveillance.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:08.200
Swallowed fire hot sauce the other day.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.810
Fire sauce made me cough and aiee.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.940
Cough-ee by fire sauce.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.280
Coffee by a fire source.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.390
What's this about a fire sauce?

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:18.200
There's no point in asking.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.930
If we could use this thing, we could talk to everybody,

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.210
but Omoikane has to...

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:28.420
Nergal's no pushover, so they probably reprogrammed Omoikane to be obedient to them.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.330
Since these terminals don't work anymore, it looks like...

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:33.970
This sounds like something Ruri-Ruri would say,

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.900
but it looks like the Nadesico is no longer the Nadesico.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.490
And so, we the crew...

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.040
All separated, you mean?

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:43.830
Hey, why can't the two of us enjoy our second take at life?

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.410
With surveillance, of course.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.560
How long is this going to last?

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:51.080
Probably until the secret is no longer a secret.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:54.140
The veil of secrecy lifted, Earth and Jupiter reconciled,

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.740
we stride forth into boundless space!

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.160
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:58.400 --> 00:09:59.330
Once the fighting ends,

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:03.290
the two learn to work together as comrades toward building a better future for all.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.160
Or that's the golden conclusion for cartoons and movies, but...

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.110
Well, what can you do?

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:08.520
I suppose.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.170
I humbly submit this to you, Sir.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:12.010
Well, it doesn't look too bad.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.520
You need another ten years.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:28.000
But these are times when hacks who should train for another hundred years

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.770
get big places and sport big attitudes.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:31.840
Good enough. You've passed.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.070
Really, Sir?

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:34.460
You passed.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.270
Thank you so much, Master.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.780
Looks like you stopped running.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.200
What? I'm still running, actually.

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:44.550
Idiot, I meant, you stopped running from yourself.

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:47.530
You must've been under one hell of a chef.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:49.410
Yes, Sir!

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:51.540
Now you're a true cook.

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.510
You are a peculiar one. Why did you stay?

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.140
My contract's not up yet, and because I felt like it.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.230
Think it's too late to run?

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.450
Do you still have to care for that kitten?

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:06.430
I guess so.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:19.610
Unforgettable Days
for Those
Living Now

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.620
Megum-sani! Megumi-san!

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.430
Yes, Ruri here.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:38.770
Meow.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.140
What the hell?

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.310
I hope all of you are doing fine.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.450
Ruri-chan...

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:50.230
What is this?

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.440
This feed's audio and visual signals have been slightly altered

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.620
so that only you can receive this transmission.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.010
Because of this, there might be some degradation.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.910
I'm sorry I have not been able to communicate with you sooner.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:05.860
I was having a difficult time getting Omoikane

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:07.910
to act out the personality in Nergal's replacement programming.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:10.570
A computer was acting out a part?

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:15.280
Yes, but Omoikane does not like pretending to be someone else, so it wasn't easy for me.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:15.840
How strange.

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.430
But I needed to let all of you know this.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:21.010
The Nadesico is still alive.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.930
Ruri-Ruri, if you're dressed like that, it must be cold there.

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:28.170
Yes, but since I borrowed this outfit from Houmei-san, I'm fine.

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:29.800
I'm more resilient than you think.

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.190
Ruri-Ruri is smiling!

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:37.440
Somebody said long ago that, "the Nadesico is your ship."

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.230
That's how I feel now as well.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:42.700
This ship

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.370
is our ship.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.270
Looks like it's time that I laid in more supplies.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.790
Everyone, time to change our aprons.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:54.950
Change?

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:55.980
Yes!

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:58.770
Check all Aestivalis systems.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.060
Yeah, let's do it.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.130
Must go, must-ard, must do.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:04.910
Hey, Akito, did you hear it? See it? What do we do?

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:05.220
Let's go!

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.140
I'm coming too!

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.560
I have to say that you really surprised me.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:15.890
Coming back all of a sudden, a year after I threw you out.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.720
With four women along with you, no less.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.150
I'm really a man.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.660
I have faith in your fried rice.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.100
My place won't do as well without you gals helping me out with your beautiful presence.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:29.990
All of you, take care of yourselves.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.080
You too.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:31.770
Take care, Sir.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.100
You work hard, all right?

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.920
Guess it looks better without me in the frame.

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:47.660
I can't let this be.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.750
As long as I am who I am.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:05.520
Ramen

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.950
Mister, where are you heading?

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:10.480
You need to ask? To the Nadesico, of course.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:13.870
Would you mind letting me pass?

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.280
Must you make this difficult?

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.860
We're going to do some rough work now, okay, Omoikane?

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:25.300
Let's move along now.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.220
Aye, aye!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.980
I'm terribly sorry about this.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:34.770
What the hell?

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:39.320
Nergal people, UEAF people, I'm sorry about this.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:40.400
Please keep quiet for a short while.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:43.640
All the shutters inside the building are closing on their own?

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:44.530
We can't control any of them!

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.290
Damn! It won't open!

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.550
Hey, open this now!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.270
All right, let's go!

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:54.970
Roger!

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:57.980
The Nadesico's mutinied?

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:00.840
What can a ship without its master key do?

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:03.720
The Nadesico's computer has hacked into many systems.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:06.720
Several former crew members seem to have infiltrated the dock in the confusion.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.850
The confusion will be temporary.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:12.860
They can't launch. We have the master key.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.900
Jun-kun, how much further do we have to go to the Nadesico?

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.270
Captain! We've come for you!

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.800
Is everyone all right?

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:32.900
Are YOU all right?

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.210
Captain, over here! Tenkawa, cover me!

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.920
Look at your radar!

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:42.910
"Ack!" my ass!

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:47.050
What is so funny?

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.390
Damn, I certainly did not see this coming.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:54.930
I thought Goat Hory was just another stiff, but there was much more to him than I ever imagined.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:55.640
Was?

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:56.100
Got the key.
Goat Hory

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.830
He took off with the master key.

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:02.810
Here you go, eat up!

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:04.650
Tastes great.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.560
How much longer is it going to be until Ryoko gets here?

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.410
The hard part is just beginning.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:18.690
We need to retrieve everyone from all over.

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:21.670
But before we can do that, there are those we need here first.

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:23.920
Hey mister, a boiled egg next.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.000
Hey mister, another bowl.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:31.970
Bastards! Look at 'em go at us knowing we can't shoot back...

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.220
Come on, Ryoko-chan. Haste makes things worse.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.850
It's only a little further to Hiratsuka.

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.310
Man, you're ruining the cockpit mood.

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:40.090
Whoops.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.720
I was actually thinking, running a ramen shop might be nice.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.580
To help run a ramen shop alongside Akito...

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:50.150
I'll be the pretty waitress that's the talk of the town.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:53.630
Akito would be the young but really skillful cook.

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:57.120
A small but popular restaurant...

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:05.010
But I guess that's not enough for Akito.
Not enough for me either.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:09.460
That ship just means so much to him, and to me as well.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:13.340
Right! Let's go, Captain!

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:13.680
Yes!

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:18.690
I repeat! Give yourselves up!

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:20.140
We will guarantee your safety!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:22.160
Guarantee what safety after this?

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.800
Liars, liars, liars!

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.380
Crooks start out as liars!

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:27.060
Damn!

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.230
We will guarantee your safety!

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:35.240
So you'll even open fire inside cities, you jerks!

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.070
Made it, Captain!

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:39.490
Okay!

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:41.470
You're late, Ryoko.

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:43.410
So late, so narrow, so dark, on this path...

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:45.080
I'm back!

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:45.990
Here you are.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:47.680
We will launch immediately!

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.420
Everyone to your stations please.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:57.060
Raising distortion field.

00:17:57.390 --> 00:17:58.880
Auxiliary engine online.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.120
Sorry I'm late!

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.350
Opening communication channels.

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:03.600
Megumi-chan...

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.610
We will begin the retrieval of our crew.

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:09.270
First, set course for Akito's location!

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:16.160
Tenkawa unit, currently moving outside the gravitron wave range.

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:23.800
Bastards must figure that we won't shoot back.

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:26.070
They're bad guys, who cares? Shoot them down, shoot them down!

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.210
No killing!

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.320
At most the battery will last us another thirty minutes.

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:31.720
All we can do is run.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:33.600
The Aestivalis is recharging.

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:38.720
Sorry to make you wait, Akito.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.640
You were pretty fast.

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:42.310
I rushed for your sake.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:50.560
Seiya, going off chasing after women again?

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.860
I'm sorry. I have friends waiting for me.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.450
Friends that need me for my expertise as a mechanic.

00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:59.160
When will you be back next?

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:00.650
I don't know...

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.180
It might be tomorrow. It might be ten years from now.

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:07.000
But I will come back for sure.

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:09.420
Take care of yourself.

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:13.340
Jeez, just look at how you abuse these babies!

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:14.340
I'm sorry.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:14.570
Had to happen.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:15.200
Uripee.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:15.410
Had to happen.

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:16.760
We'll be counting on you again, man.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:18.410
Hey, same goes for me as well.

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:20.220
Altitude two hundred kilometers.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.650
We will go ahead and punch out of Earth's atmosphere!

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:24.640
Last time, this is where we got hit by the missiles.

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:27.410
Defense systems have a thing called a cancel code.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:28.480
Here we go!

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:32.400
Utilizing communication satellites to hack into all defense systems.

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:38.050
Forth Defensive Line

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.240
Why aren't the missiles being fired?!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.680
A cancel code has been introduced to the defense system!

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:42.160
What?!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:42.610
This is space station Sakura.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.240
Space station "Sakura" - Delphinium Hanger

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:46.190
The Delphinium wing cannot launch!

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:47.440
The Nadesico has reached an altitude of 30,000 kilometers!

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:49.560
UEAF Command HQ

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:49.920
The Nadesico has reached an altitude of 30,000 kilometers!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.850
The Big Barrier system is not responding!

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.690
Combined crew of one hundred three on board.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.840
Where are we headed to, Captain?

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:59.040
Our destination is clear!

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.430
We head to where Yukina-chan's brother is.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:01.760
Onii-chan, wait for me!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.600
Your lovely Yukina will be by your side in no time.

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:05.010
Do we have a destination?

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:07.910
If we head toward Jupiter, we're sure to find him!

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:12.100
Obviously.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.420
Looks like the Nadesico's taken off.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:22.720
The slogan, "Personalities aside, the best crew compliment ever" was no joke in the case of that ship.

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:25.950
Can't be helped. We need to start preparing as well.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.640
The Kakitsubata's ready to go, right?

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:29.460
Yes.

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:32.700
This is going to get quite interesting.

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.250
For both us and them.

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:37.150
Isn't that right, Doctor?

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:46.880
Emergency notification!

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.530
A special event for the wildly popular television anime show

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.710
"Hot Blooded Robot Gekiganger 3" has been announced!

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:52.380
It will be named Gekiganger Festival.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:53.280
Nicknamed the Geki-Fes.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.590
For more information, please call the Geki-Fes Operations Committee.

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:58.410
The number to call is "Nadesico 00 123 Gekiganger".

00:21:58.410 --> 00:21:59.330
And so,

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.230
Friends of justice, Gekiganger,
Friends of justice, Gekiganger,

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:04.680
We can't stop loving you, Gekiganger,
We can't stop loving you, Gekiganger,

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:07.420
Gekigan

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:10.720
Gekiganger!
